# LF-stable text for research artifacts (protocols, schemas, ledgers, scripts,
# and dossiers). HC-CORTEX-002's raw JSONL ledgers are content-addressed
# hash-chains; verifyLedgerBytes() (scripts/hc-cortex-002-evidence-lib.mjs)
# fails closed on any CR byte (LEDGER_FRAMING_INVALID), and every produced
# JSON/JSONL artifact is LF-terminated by construction. A CRLF-normalizing
# checkout (Windows core.autocrlf=true without this file) would silently
# corrupt those digests on clone. Git's own gitattributes documentation
# recommends this exact baseline: https://git-scm.com/docs/gitattributes
* text=auto eol=lf

*.json text eol=lf
*.jsonl text eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf
*.mjs text eol=lf
*.py text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf

# No binary research artifact is committed to this repository today (raw
# SQLite databases and PostgreSQL clusters are runtime-generated, never
# checked in); these entries exist so a future binary addition does not
# silently fall through text normalization.
*.sqlite3 binary
*.db binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.pdf binary
